# Settings for ONE robot of several. Copy once per robot to .env.<name> (for example
# .env.one and .env.two), fill in the values marked FILL IN, and name the file in every
# command for that robot:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.one up -d bridge
# See docs/two-robots.md. With a single robot, use .env.example instead.

# --- This robot -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Its name and address on the network (see .env.example for how to find them).
# FILL IN
ROBOT_HOSTNAME=011xxxPxxxx.local
# FILL IN
ROBOT_IP=192.168.x.x
# ROBOT_HOSTNAME_2=011xxxPxxxx.local
# FILL IN (same name as ROBOT_HOSTNAME)
ROS_MASTER_URI=http://011xxxPxxxx.local:11311
# Only if this robot stands on a Mobility Base whose own computer runs programs of the
# robot's ROS 1 system: that computer's name and address (see .env.example; the inventory
# lists such computers in machines.txt).
# BASE_HOSTNAME=name-of-the-base-computer
# BASE_IP=192.168.x.x
# Only for MoveIt: 1 for an arm with Rethink's electric gripper (see .env.example).
# LEFT_ELECTRIC_GRIPPER=0
# RIGHT_ELECTRIC_GRIPPER=0

# --- This machine -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This machine's address on the network THIS robot is on (the same in every robot's file
# if all robots are on one network).
# FILL IN
ROS_IP=192.168.x.x

# --- What keeps the robots apart --------------------------------------------------------------
# This robot's name. All Baxters use the same topic names; the bridge puts this name in
# front of them in ROS 2, so the first robot's joint states are /one/robot/joint_states.
# In programs: baxter_interface.Robot('one'). Letters, digits and single underscores,
# starting with a letter. Use the same name as in the file's name.
# FILL IN
ROBOT_NAME=NAME

# A name for this robot's containers, so that the bridges of two robots can run next to
# each other. Use "baxter-" and the robot's name.
# FILL IN
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=baxter-NAME

# Where this robot stands in the room, for pictures that show all robots together
# (docs/rviz.md): x, y and z in metres from a point you choose (the same point for all
# robots, for example the first robot's place), and the turn in degrees around the
# vertical axis, counter-clockwise seen from above. x points forward from that point,
# y to the left. The first robot: 0 0 0 0. A second one 1.5 m to its left, facing the
# same way: 0 1.5 0 0. MEASURE IT; the picture is only as right as these numbers.
ROBOT_POSITION=0 0 0 0

# The ROS 2 domain. THE SAME NUMBER FOR ALL ROBOTS (and as in .env.example): they are
# meant to be seen together, the names keep them apart.
ROS_DOMAIN_ID=42

# --- As in .env.example -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# A robot with a name works in fixed_list mode only.
BRIDGE_MODE=fixed_list
# PROJECT_DIR=/home/you/my_baxter_programs
# DDS_PROFILE=wsl
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.wsl-gpu.yaml
